==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Balalan Pasalan''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Piccolan Pasalan''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
This form is <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other cats from Tales of the Nekoluga, this cat is not meant to be used until it evolves.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Balalan Pasalan's damage is abysmally low, but its long-ranged freeze can be used to great effect as support, giving other units more time to attack.

Another use for it would be to stop long-ranged enemies that can constantly attack your units while they are being approached, such as [[Camelle]] or [[Master A.|Master A]]. If you have money to spare, you could use this tactic along with a bunch of [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|rushers]] such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]. Speaking of Awakened Bahamut, Balalan Pasalan's effect makes it less difficult to clip him past enemies with [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper the Cat]] or the [[Cat Cannon]], which can be used to cheese stages that have only a singular main threat.

Balalan Pasalan forms a powerful combo with [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] and [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Recruit]]. Cyberpunk Cat can slow down incoming enemies, Balalan Pasalan can tame enemies that enter Cyberpunk's blindspot and further impede enemies that are in Cyberpunk's range if he gets close enough, and Sniper the Recruit can help regain ground for the other 2 with his Knockback and (in [[True Form]]) slow.

On the flip side, Balalan Pasalan has a long delay between attacks, meaning it shouldn't be used as your only source of crowd-control in a level, unless the level doesn't require it.

==='''True Form'''===
Piccolan Pasalan gains weaken and has its freeze duration increased to a total 3 seconds, doubling its value. The weaken duration is 6 seconds, but effectively only 3, since during the first 3 seconds of the weaken duration the enemy will be stopped anyway, unless the enemy is immune to freeze. This combo of abilities proves very useful for enemies with powerful attacks, as the freeze time will give your cats some time to hit without being hit back. The freeze increase is especially notable for rapid attackers such as the aforementioned [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] and [[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat.]] The weaken afterward will help halve the damage taken after the freeze wears off for 3 seconds. Like its previous form, it should be shielded heavily due to its low health. Overall, worth the investment.

==='''Talents'''===
Piccolan Pasalan's Talents generally aren't worth investing in, due to serving no utility for a unit of this caliber.

'''Wave Resist''' and '''Surge Resist''' are in the right direction, as they tend to negate the unit's extreme range advantage, with the former being the most prevalent as Surges rarely reach it in the first place. Unfortunately, its low base health and long cooldown means it can't afford to absorb enough without total immunity to them. Similarly, '''Survive''' and '''HP Buff''' just doesn't have the consistency, due to maxing out at 50% chance and not adding enough to the unit's nonexistent survivability. '''Weaken''' also doesn't work at all with the long attack cycle, as for its massive NP cost it only increases the ability's duration by one second.

==='''Orbs'''===
'''Wave Resist''' and '''Surge Resist''' [[Talent Orbs|Ability orbs]] pair well with prior wave/surge resist talents to make Balaluga wave/surge immune.

