==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Balaluga was a part of two other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Legend of the Nekoluga (Removed Combo)|Legend of the Nekoluga]] and [[Nekoluganomicon (Removed Combo)|Nekoluganomicon]].
*Ironically, Balaluga has higher attack power and DPS than its evolutions.
*Balalan Pasalan has the lowest attack power of any [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]].
*Balalan Pasalan has the fourth-lowest DPS out of all Cats in the game, with only 11 DPS at level 30, which is even lower than [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Cleanerbot Cat's]] 32 DPS at level 30. [[Million-Dollar Cat (Special Cat)|Million-Dollar Cat]] has lower DPS than both, having only 6 DPS at level 30. [[Healer (Special Cat)|Healer]] also has lower DPS, having 4 DPS at level 30. However, with a many-way tie, the champions for lowest DPS are the [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Eggs]], with 2.17 DPS at level 30.
*Balaluga is the only [[Tales of the Nekoluga (Gacha Event)|Luga]] without traditional cat ears.
*Piccolan Pasalan takes up so much of its icon that the golden hue is hardly visible (if you have a good eye, you will see it at the bottom-left corner).
*Balalan and [[Nekoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Nekoluga]] are currently the only Tales of the Nekoluga units to have seasonal variants, with [[Betrothed Balaluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Betrothed Balaluga]] and [[Summerluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Summerluga]] respectively.
*Its name indicates that he has separate limbs/body parts. Bala-luga might be taken from ''bara'' (ばらばら, ''bara bara''), an onomatopoeic word that is used to express scatter/separate/split, or, perhaps, ''hara'' (ばら, stomach).
*"Piccolan" is derived from the Japanese word ''pika'' (ぴか), an onomatopoeic word for something that is flashing or glittering, referencing its attack.
*Balalan Pasalan resembles the legendary [[wikipedia:Headless men|Blemmyes]], a headless tribe whose faces are on their chests.
*Piccolan Pasalan's design references the Angel [[The 4th Angel (Enemy)|The 4th Angel]] from the anime ''[[wikipedia:Neon Genesis Evangelion|Neon Genesis Evangelion]]''. Similarities include the red core in the center of their bodies, the flaps on the sides of their heads, the "lances" inside their arms, and the rib-like bones clutching their core, in addition to having similar body shapes. Its description states that it may be an extraterrestrial of unfathomable power, further referencing the Angels from the series.

